    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48448" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tĭtŭbātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				staggering</i>, <i>wavering.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in ipsā ebrietate,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 95, 16</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">linguae,</span>”
				i. e. <i>stammering</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 7, 6 <i>med.</i></span></i>
			; cf. the preced. art.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">titubatio aut offensio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Auct. Her. 2, 8, 12</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Cic. Inv. 2, 12, 41</span></i>; Hier. de Cain et
			Abel, 1, 5, 19.</div>
